From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] msvcp60: Implement std::bad_typeid, std::__non_rtti_object, std::bad_exception and ios_base::exceptions(short).

msvcp60's own std::bad_typeid, std::__non_rtti_object and
std::bad_exception (beside the CRT's global classes): constructors from
a message, default constructor closures, copy constructors,
assignments, destructors, vtables (exported data) and _Doraise (the
shared FIXME); and ios_base::exceptions with the state as a short. Also
maps ARM names whose i386 twins are implemented.
---
 dlls/msvcp60/ios.c        |  12 ++++
 dlls/msvcp60/msvcp60.spec | 108 ++++++++++++++++++------------------
 dlls/msvcp90/exception.c  | 138 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 204 insertions(+), 54 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dlls/msvcp60/ios.c b/dlls/msvcp60/ios.c
index 0c3cc1a..21e6891 100644
--- a/dlls/msvcp60/ios.c
+++ b/dlls/msvcp60/ios.c
@@ -3832,6 +3832,18 @@ void __thiscall ios_base_exceptions_set(ios_base *this, IOSB_iostate state)
     ios_base_clear(this, this->state);
 }
 
+/* ?exceptions@ios_base@std@@QAEXF@Z */
+/* ?exceptions@ios_base@std@@QEAAXF@Z */
+/* the overload with the state as a short */
+DEFINE_THISCALL_WRAPPER(ios_base_exceptions_set_short, 8)
+void __thiscall ios_base_exceptions_set_short(ios_base *this, short state)
+{
+#ifdef SG_MUTANT_EXCEPTIONS_SHORT_NOP
+    return;
+#endif
+    ios_base_exceptions_set(this, state);
+}
+
 /* ?exceptions@ios_base@std@@QBEHXZ */
 /* ?exceptions@ios_base@std@@QEBAHXZ */
 DEFINE_THISCALL_WRAPPER(ios_base_exceptions_get, 4)
